  "final_answer": "I have gathered all the necessary information about the latest updated image-to-video model on HuggingFace. Here is my final answer:\n\n## Latest Updated Image-to-Video Model on HuggingFace\n\n**Model:** `KevinDavies/Wan2.2-S2V-14B`\n\nThis model was the most recently updated in the \"Image-to-Video\" pipeline category on HuggingFace, appearing first in the sort-by-modified list. It was released on **August 26, 2025**.\n\n### Basic Information\n- **Publisher:** KevinDavies\n- **Task:** Image-to-Video\n- **Library:** Diffusers\n- **Format:** Safetensors\n- **Model Size:** 16B parameters\n- **Tensor Type:** BF16\n- **Language:** Spanish\n- **License:** Apache-2.0\n- **Tags:** s2v\n- **Related Papers:** arXiv:2508.18621, arXiv:2503.20314\n\n### Description\nThe model is designed for **audio-driven cinematic video generation** (Wan-S2V: Audio-Driven Cinematic Video Generation).\n\n### Main Features\n\n**1. Audio-Driven Cinematic Video Generation**\n- Built specifically to handle complex film and television production scenarios requiring nuanced character interactions, realistic body movements, and dynamic camera work — going beyond typical speech/singing animation.\n- Benchmarked against Hunyuan-Avatar and Omnihuman, with results showing it significantly outperforms these existing solutions.\n- Also supports long-form video generation and precise video lip-sync editing.\n\n**2. Effective MoE (Mixture-of-Experts) Architecture**\n- Introduces an MoE architecture into video diffusion models, separating the denoising process across timesteps with specialized expert models.\n- Enlarges overall model capacity while maintaining the same computational cost.\n\n**3. Cinematic-Level Aesthetics**\n- Trained on meticulously curated aesthetic data with detailed labels for lighting, composition, contrast, color tone, and more.\n- Enables more precise and controllable cinematic style generation with customizable aesthetic preferences.\n\n**4. Complex Motion Generation**\n- Trained on a significantly larger dataset compared to Wan2.1: **+65.6% more images** and **+83.2% more videos**.\n- Improves generalization across motions, semantics, and aesthetics dimensions.\n\n**5. Efficient High-Definition Hybrid TI2V (sibling model)**\n- 5B model variant with Wan2.2-VAE achieving compression ratio of **16×16×4**.\n- Supports both text-to-video and image-to-video generation at **720P resolution @ 24fps**.\n- Can run on consumer-grade GPUs like the RTX 4090, making it one of the fastest 720P@24fps models available.",
